# Choices of the 2025-26 zoo that no axis settles, one change at a time from the 2021
# reference, GPT-3's decoder with RoPE (gpt3_rope.bux). The zoo disagrees on how far
# and how often its layers look: attention.bux's `swa` (3 layers of 4 see 512 keys)
# is one point, and these arms move its window, its ratio, its sinks and its global
# layers' positions, so compare them with `swa` as well as with the reference. The
# others are the gate's form, a norm without statistics, and how much of a hybrid is
# linear (mixers.bux's `kda` is KDA in 3 layers of 4). Arms: era, source, what it was
# claimed for.
use gpt3_rope
use timeline_code
use rungs

layer(a) = [norm a] [norm ffn]
lm(a)    = embed layer(a)^layers norm head(tied=true)
local(w) = layer(attn(sliding_window_size=w))
G        = block

# The sparsest ratio of local to global layers in the zoo that the depth divides: 7:1
# in the 8 layers of d512 (MiMo-V2.6), 5:1 in the 12 of d768 (Inkling, Beam 1.0).
sparse = d512: 7 | d768: 5 | d1024: 7 | d1280: 9

# DyT in place of every norm after the embedding e, alpha from a.
dyt_lm(e, a) = e ([dyt(alpha_init=a) attn] [dyt(alpha_init=a) ffn])^layers
               dyt(alpha_init=a) head(tied=true)

# mixers.bux's KDA: query and key heads of 128, as wide together as the stream, twice
# as many value heads, the decay bounded at -5 as Kimi K3's.
K = layer(kda(num_heads=d_model // 128, num_v_heads=d_model // 64, head_dim=128,
              gate_lower_bound=-5))

model = # 2026 Trinity, Beam 1.0, Muse Spark, Command A+, North Mini Code: swa's local
        # layers, its global layers without positions; long context
        swa_nope:   embed (local(512)^3 layer(attn(rope=none)))^(layers // 4)
                    norm head(tied=true)
      # 2025 Qwen3-Next, 2026 Qwen3.8, MiMo-V2.6, MiniMax-M3: swa's global layers
      # rotate a quarter of the dims at base 10M, which YaRN extends; long context
      | swa_prope:  embed (local(512)^3
                           layer(attn(rope=rope(base=10000000, fraction=0.25))))^(layers // 4)
                    norm head(tied=true)
      # 2025 gpt-oss, 2026 MiMo-V2.6: swa with a learned sink logit per head in every
      # layer; long context, stability of the local layers
      | swa_sinks:  embed (layer(attn(sliding_window_size=512, sinks=true))^3
                           layer(attn(sinks=true)))^(layers // 4)
                    norm head(tied=true)
      # 2025 gpt-oss, 2026 MiMo-V2.6, DeepSeek-V4.1's window: swa with a window of
      # 128; KV cache, throughput
      | swa_128:    embed (local(128)^3 G)^(layers // 4) norm head(tied=true)
      # 2026 Muse Spark: swa with a window of 2048, the rows' length, so it differs
      # from the reference in the 16k phase alone; long context at a bounded cache
      | swa_2048:   embed (local(2048)^3 G)^(layers // 4) norm head(tied=true)
      # 2024 Gemma 2, 2025 gpt-oss: swa in every other layer; quality at a bounded cache
      | swa_1to1:   embed (local(512) G)^(layers // 2) norm head(tied=true)
      # 2025 Gemma 3, 2026 Inkling, Beam 1.0, MiMo-V2.6: swa with one global layer in
      # 8 at d512, in 6 at d768; KV cache, throughput
      | swa_sparse: embed (local(512)^sparse G)^(layers // (sparse + 1))
                    norm head(tied=true)
      # 2026 Laguna XS 2.1: a softplus gate, one value per head, on every head's
      # output; attention.bux's `gated` has one per channel, by a sigmoid; stability
      | gate_head:  lm(attn(gated=true, gate_per_head=true, gate_activation=softplus))
      # 2025 Zhu et al. (DyT): tanh(alpha x) with a gain and a bias in place of every
      # LayerNorm, no statistics; throughput
      | dyt:        embed ([dyt attn] [dyt ffn])^layers dyt head(tied=true)
      # dyt with alpha starting at 0.05, 0.1 and 0.2: the paper's LLMs take a smaller
      # one the wider they are; does a smaller one train?
      | dyt_a005:   dyt_lm(embed, 0.05)
      | dyt_a01:    dyt_lm(embed, 0.1)
      | dyt_a02:    dyt_lm(embed, 0.2)
      # dyt with the embedding scaled by sqrt(d_model), so that the tanh reads inputs
      # of order 1 where a norm would (embeddings start at 0.02); alpha from 0.5 and 0.2
      | dyt_emb:    dyt_lm(embed(scale_by_sqrt_dim=true), 0.5)
      | dyt_emb_a02: dyt_lm(embed(scale_by_sqrt_dim=true), 0.2)
      # 2024 Gemma 2's ratio, 2025 Kimi Linear's 1:1 ablation: KDA in every other
      # layer; quality, the hybrid's cost of attention
      | kda_1to1:   embed (K G)^(layers // 2) norm head(tied=true)
      # 2024 Jamba, 2025 MiniMax-01, Nemotron-H: KDA in all but one layer in 8 at
      # d512, in 6 at d768; long-context cost
      | kda_sparse: embed (K^sparse G)^(layers // (sparse + 1)) norm head(tied=true)
